1
00:00:08,530 --> 00:00:10,570
[ERWIN]
Let's move!

2
00:00:19,880 --> 00:00:22,450
[HANGE grunts]

3
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:23,810
Hange?

4
00:00:23,850 --> 00:00:26,320
Get, get me a horse.

5
00:00:26,350 --> 00:00:29,650
Section Commander!
Where're you going?

6
00:00:29,690 --> 00:00:31,190
Back to the village
where we caught

7
00:00:31,220 --> 00:00:33,320
the Titan that couldn't walk.

8
00:00:33,360 --> 00:00:34,990
Not Ragako!

9
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:37,390
I need to see.

10
00:00:37,460 --> 00:00:39,530
Have you lost touch
with reality?

11
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:43,530
You're in no condition
to ride horseback right now!

12
00:00:44,800 --> 00:00:46,570
There's something
important there.

13
00:00:46,640 --> 00:00:49,010
I feel it in my bones.

14
00:00:51,440 --> 00:00:54,510
All right, fine.

15
00:00:54,550 --> 00:00:55,980
I'll go myself.

16
00:00:56,010 --> 00:00:59,050
You stay here
and quit trying to move!

17
00:01:04,390 --> 00:01:08,230
Be on the lookout!
All riders assume formation!

18
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:20,000
[MIKASA]
Eren.

19
00:01:20,570 --> 00:01:25,580
♪ Opening Song

20
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:01,420
[REINER]
You're awake.

21
00:03:01,490 --> 00:03:03,360
Welcome back.

22
00:03:12,270 --> 00:03:14,470
[Gasps]

23
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:21,740
[Breathe heavily]

24
00:03:21,780 --> 00:03:26,110
[Gasps]
What the hell? My arms!

25
00:03:26,180 --> 00:03:27,880
[YMIR]
Eren.

26
00:03:27,920 --> 00:03:31,280
I'm, uh, not in any
better shape here.

27
00:03:31,350 --> 00:03:34,090
Seems we're both
having a shit day.

28
00:03:34,120 --> 00:03:39,060
Ymir. What did they...
What did they do to me?

29
00:03:39,090 --> 00:03:44,400
[REINER] Sorry. That was...
That was my fault.

30
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:46,730
You can pin
your injuries on me.

31
00:03:46,770 --> 00:03:49,200
Guess I was in kind of
a hurry back there.

32
00:03:49,240 --> 00:03:55,110
Bit your nape without
thinking about your arms.

33
00:03:55,140 --> 00:04:01,180
Is that right? So. I lost.

34
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:12,130
Eren! Don't do it!

35
00:04:12,160 --> 00:04:14,590
Easy there, hothead.

36
00:04:14,630 --> 00:04:17,060
Take a look at where we are.

37
00:04:17,100 --> 00:04:20,630
This is the giant forest
within Wall Maria.

38
00:04:20,670 --> 00:04:24,270
Wall Rose is leagues away.

39
00:04:24,310 --> 00:04:26,340
Which means...
we're deep in the heart

40
00:04:26,410 --> 00:04:29,940
of Titan country. See?

41
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:33,080
I think our buddy
down there is an abnormal.

42
00:04:33,120 --> 00:04:35,820
It may look like
he's just kickin' back,

43
00:04:35,850 --> 00:04:39,420
but those eyes
haven't left us once.

44
00:04:39,450 --> 00:04:41,760
Lot of smaller ones
down there, too.

45
00:04:41,790 --> 00:04:46,960
That's plenty bad enough.
Another big one over there.

46
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,700
Fixated but
keeping his distance.

47
00:04:49,770 --> 00:04:53,330
Strikes me as the shy type.

48
00:04:53,370 --> 00:04:55,800
And then there are
these chumps.

49
00:04:55,840 --> 00:04:57,700
Dirty bastards.

50
00:04:57,770 --> 00:05:00,810
They had the foresight
to suit up in full gear.

51
00:05:00,840 --> 00:05:04,110
'Course Reiner took yours.

52
00:05:04,150 --> 00:05:06,210
Point is, changing into
a Titan isn't gonna

53
00:05:06,280 --> 00:05:08,680
accomplish very much right now.

54
00:05:08,720 --> 00:05:11,020
One, they can do
the same thing if they want.

55
00:05:11,050 --> 00:05:13,950
Two, they can zip
into the trees if not.

56
00:05:13,990 --> 00:05:17,390
Three, we're basically
surrounded on all sides.

57
00:05:17,460 --> 00:05:20,490
Power or no power, getting out
of this would be tricky as hell,

58
00:05:20,530 --> 00:05:24,130
even at the best of times.

59
00:05:24,170 --> 00:05:25,670
Y'read me?

60
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:28,640
There's nothing to gain
by being a dumbass.

61
00:05:28,670 --> 00:05:30,540
[REINER]
She's right.

62
00:05:30,570 --> 00:05:33,470
Y'can't turn into Titans
right now anyway.

63
00:05:33,510 --> 00:05:37,080
Don't count on that ability
coming to the rescue.

64
00:05:37,150 --> 00:05:39,350
The body can only take so much.

65
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:42,850
It's a little preoccupied
with healing at the moment.

66
00:05:44,390 --> 00:05:47,020
Nice try. You expect
me to sit here

67
00:05:47,060 --> 00:05:49,820
and take the word of liar?

68
00:05:52,830 --> 00:05:56,030
Yeah, well. We're sort of
at a disadvantage here.

69
00:05:56,060 --> 00:05:59,100
It's not like we know the ins
and outs of how this works.

70
00:05:59,170 --> 00:06:01,570
Unlike you guys,
I'm basically clueless

71
00:06:01,600 --> 00:06:03,600
about the whole thing.

72
00:06:03,670 --> 00:06:05,840
Hey, Reiner.

73
00:06:05,870 --> 00:06:09,280
You said you'd start
talking once Eren was up.

74
00:06:09,340 --> 00:06:11,510
Don't'cha think it's
about time somebody explains

75
00:06:11,550 --> 00:06:13,850
what you plan on doing with us?

76
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:19,050
[REINER] We're taking you
to our hometown.

77
00:06:19,090 --> 00:06:23,190
Of course, I realize neither of
you is just gonna do as I ask.

78
00:06:23,230 --> 00:06:24,920
Like Ymir was saying, though,

79
00:06:24,960 --> 00:06:30,130
this place is crawling with
Titans. They're everywhere.

80
00:06:30,200 --> 00:06:32,030
We could beat the living
shit out of each other

81
00:06:32,070 --> 00:06:34,270
if that's what you want.

82
00:06:34,340 --> 00:06:36,300
But I wouldn't recommend it.

83
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:38,170
Our friends
down below are hungry

84
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:40,440
and not prone to discriminate.

85
00:06:40,480 --> 00:06:42,910
[REINER] Whether you try to
cut and run or stick around,

86
00:06:42,940 --> 00:06:46,380
believe me when I say
our options are limited.

87
00:06:46,410 --> 00:06:49,650
We wait for nightfall.

88
00:06:49,720 --> 00:06:51,480
So, why didn't you
just stay in Titan form

89
00:06:51,550 --> 00:06:53,090
and run all the way home?

90
00:06:53,120 --> 00:06:55,890
What's the point of stopping
here in the first place?

91
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:59,290
You get winded
and have to take a break?

92
00:06:59,330 --> 00:07:02,160
Why don't you
use your imagination?

93
00:07:02,230 --> 00:07:04,330
[YMIR sighs]

94
00:07:05,770 --> 00:07:09,840
[EREN] Let me think.
Suppose I wait for an opening.

95
00:07:09,910 --> 00:07:12,770
If I assume Titan form,
running away wouldn't really

96
00:07:12,810 --> 00:07:15,410
be that much of a challenge.

97
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:21,310
Question is, can I assume
Titan form in this condition?

98
00:07:21,350 --> 00:07:24,020
Reiner doesn't seem to think so,

99
00:07:24,090 --> 00:07:25,920
and it's not like he
and Bertholdt would risk

100
00:07:25,950 --> 00:07:29,120
stopping here
without a good reason.

101
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:32,390
What if I couldn't
transform to full strength?

102
00:07:32,430 --> 00:07:36,030
Does that mean the other Titans
would be able to eat me?

103
00:07:37,470 --> 00:07:39,030
So we're just gonna
sit on our asses

104
00:07:39,100 --> 00:07:40,670
till the sun goes down?

105
00:07:40,700 --> 00:07:42,340
[REINER]
It's a possibility.

106
00:07:42,370 --> 00:07:46,340
[EREN] No. Why give us
the chance to recover?

107
00:07:46,370 --> 00:07:50,840
If they wait for nightfall
we'd only be harder to rein in.

108
00:07:50,880 --> 00:07:54,480
They'll make their move
while we're still helpless.

109
00:07:56,020 --> 00:08:01,020
At this rate I can't
do anything. We're screwed.

110
00:08:01,060 --> 00:08:03,020
[Gasps]

111
00:08:03,060 --> 00:08:05,290
What happened
to everyone else?

112
00:08:05,330 --> 00:08:07,630
Where are the Scouts?

113
00:08:11,470 --> 00:08:14,000
Don't tell me they're
coming here to save us.

114
00:08:14,040 --> 00:08:16,740
Oh god. If they show up,
none of 'em will--

115
00:08:16,810 --> 00:08:17,900
Wait a second.

116
00:08:17,970 --> 00:08:19,510
Those Titans at the castle
had no problem

117
00:08:19,540 --> 00:08:23,680
moving around at night.
What's stopping these guys?

118
00:08:23,710 --> 00:08:26,310
[REINER] The Titans here
can't move after dark.

119
00:08:26,350 --> 00:08:29,820
But then you know all
about that, don't you, Ymir?

120
00:08:33,250 --> 00:08:36,760
[EREN] How is it she's able
to transform into a Titan?

121
00:08:36,830 --> 00:08:40,360
Doesn't seem to catch her
off-guard like it did me.

122
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,100
What's her angle?

123
00:08:42,160 --> 00:08:44,900
Who's side is
she on in all this?

124
00:08:44,930 --> 00:08:48,300
If I thought she was
hard to read before...

125
00:08:50,710 --> 00:08:54,440
I've made up my mind.
I need information.

126
00:08:54,510 --> 00:08:56,280
Anything I can get.

127
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,750
Keep my eyes and ears open.

128
00:08:58,780 --> 00:09:03,680
When the moment comes,
make a break for it.

129
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:07,920
Before I can do that, though...

130
00:09:07,960 --> 00:09:09,260
I have to keep
my emotions in check.

131
00:09:10,860 --> 00:09:13,930
Give myself a chance
to recuperate.

132
00:09:20,860 --> 00:09:22,230
[Gunshot]

133
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:27,200
Titan spotted at three o'clock!
Use the flare!

134
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:29,900
We've got a smoke shell
fired from the right wing!

135
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:32,040
We stay the course!
Tell the right wing

136
00:09:32,080 --> 00:09:34,910
to merge with the center
and maintain direction!

137
00:09:34,940 --> 00:09:36,840
The shortest path
is our only option.

138
00:09:36,910 --> 00:09:39,810
Straight ahead.
We have until sundown!

139
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:48,090
[HANNES]
Mikasa. Hey, Mikasa. Hello?

140
00:09:48,120 --> 00:09:50,160
Stop pushing so hard.

141
00:09:50,230 --> 00:09:52,430
You're drifting up
into the vanguard.

142
00:09:52,460 --> 00:09:55,230
You wanna break
the whole formation?

143
00:09:55,270 --> 00:09:58,230
Look, I know how you feel.
But what'd I tell ya?

144
00:09:58,270 --> 00:09:59,930
Eren's not gonna
let those assholes

145
00:09:59,970 --> 00:10:01,900
get the best of him
without a fight.

146
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:03,600
Agreed?

147
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:05,640
[MIKASA]
Mm.

148
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:07,940
Kid just doesn't
have it in him to give up.

149
00:10:07,980 --> 00:10:09,980
All we gotta do
is have a little faith.

150
00:10:10,010 --> 00:10:12,750
He'll hold his own
till the rest of us get there.

151
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,720
Always has, always will.

152
00:10:40,280 --> 00:10:44,780
[YMIR sighs]
Hey, Reiner. Got any water?

153
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:48,350
Help a girl out.
I'm dying over here.

154
00:10:48,380 --> 00:10:51,020
[REINER] Sorry, there's not
a helluva a lot I can do.

155
00:10:51,050 --> 00:10:54,720
Even if it is a matter
of life and death.

156
00:10:54,790 --> 00:10:57,160
That's comforting.
Well, at least now we know

157
00:10:57,190 --> 00:11:00,260
where we stand. Sort of.

158
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:03,930
[REINER] Speaking of which.
We've been working

159
00:11:03,970 --> 00:11:09,470
our assess off. No food,
no sleep, no nothing.

160
00:11:09,510 --> 00:11:11,540
Ever since
those Titans showed up.

161
00:11:11,570 --> 00:11:13,440
That was yesterday, right?

162
00:11:13,510 --> 00:11:17,480
Man, we're lucky the wall
hasn't been destroyed.

163
00:11:17,510 --> 00:11:20,550
Still, you'd think that means
they'd give us a break.

164
00:11:20,580 --> 00:11:24,390
And don't even get me
started on promotion.

165
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:26,890
What the hell?

166
00:11:26,920 --> 00:11:28,890
What? Aww, come on.

167
00:11:28,930 --> 00:11:31,760
I don't think that's
too much to ask, do you?

168
00:11:31,830 --> 00:11:34,230
God knows we've done
our share of heavy lifting

169
00:11:34,330 --> 00:11:36,660
all things considered.

170
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:40,940
I mean, I get it,
we're soldiers. Duty first.

171
00:11:41,000 --> 00:11:44,540
It's just nice
to be acknowledged.

172
00:11:49,710 --> 00:11:51,780
You bang your head
or something?

173
00:11:51,850 --> 00:11:54,720
What're you even
talking about. Seriously?

174
00:11:54,750 --> 00:11:56,580
Ugh. Don't give me that.

175
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,090
I'm not sayin' we
storm in and demand

176
00:11:58,120 --> 00:12:00,390
the rank of captain
or anything.

177
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:02,890
[YMIR]
No. That's not what I mean.

178
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:07,060
[REINER] Oh, yeah. Where'd you
find that cannon, by the way?

179
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:10,030
I owe you one
for saving my bacon.

180
00:12:10,070 --> 00:12:11,800
[YMIR exhales]

181
00:12:11,870 --> 00:12:14,740
[REINER] Really nice of Christa
to patch me up afterwards.

182
00:12:14,770 --> 00:12:17,440
I'm starting to think me
and her might become a thing.

183
00:12:17,470 --> 00:12:18,610
[EREN]
Hey.

184
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:20,370
Right? It's not just me?

185
00:12:20,410 --> 00:12:21,780
She always treats me
like we're--

186
00:12:21,810 --> 00:12:23,710
[EREN]
Hey!

187
00:12:26,950 --> 00:12:32,790
What's wrong with you?
You've got to be kidding me.

188
00:12:32,820 --> 00:12:36,260
Huh? What're you so
pissed about all of a sudden?

189
00:12:36,290 --> 00:12:39,130
Take it easy, man. Was it
something I said, or?

190
00:12:39,200 --> 00:12:42,060
If you wanna die,
then just keep talking!

191
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:44,100
[YMIR]
Hold up, Eren.

192
00:12:44,130 --> 00:12:46,930
I think somebody's
gone off the deep end.

193
00:12:46,970 --> 00:12:50,740
Is that what this is, Bertholdt?

194
00:12:50,770 --> 00:12:52,570
If you know something we don't,

195
00:12:52,610 --> 00:12:55,610
now would be a good time
to put it on the table.

196
00:12:55,650 --> 00:12:57,250
Huh?

197
00:12:59,520 --> 00:13:02,950
[BERTHOLDT]
Reiner. Snap out of it.

198
00:13:02,990 --> 00:13:05,920
You're not a soldier, okay?

199
00:13:05,990 --> 00:13:10,420
You and I are... We're warriors.

200
00:13:10,460 --> 00:13:20,330
[REINER breathe quaveringly]

201
00:13:20,370 --> 00:13:23,100
[MARCO]
Reiner! What are you doing?

202
00:13:24,010 --> 00:13:28,640
[MARCO screams and gasps]

203
00:13:28,680 --> 00:13:31,210
[REINER]
Hey. Why...?

204
00:13:31,280 --> 00:13:33,880
[BERTHOLDT gasps]

205
00:13:33,950 --> 00:13:39,190
Why is Marco... being devoured?

206
00:13:46,530 --> 00:13:52,170
Right. I see.
That's how things are.

207
00:13:52,200 --> 00:13:57,240
[sobs softly]

208
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:03,210
What the hell's he doing?

209
00:14:03,250 --> 00:14:07,650
I have a pretty good idea.
At least I think so.

210
00:14:07,680 --> 00:14:09,520
Didn't add up at first.

211
00:14:09,550 --> 00:14:11,420
Why would the man
who broke the wall

212
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:14,590
risk his neck to save Conny?

213
00:14:14,660 --> 00:14:17,160
It's like the poor
bastard's personality is

214
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:18,890
compartmentalized.

215
00:14:18,930 --> 00:14:22,000
Everything he does is
a contradiction in terms.

216
00:14:22,030 --> 00:14:23,660
He can't help it.

217
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:25,500
On one hand,
he's a warrior bent on

218
00:14:25,540 --> 00:14:27,540
pushing mankind past the brink.

219
00:14:27,570 --> 00:14:30,270
On the other he's
pretending to be a solider.

220
00:14:30,340 --> 00:14:34,610
I'm thinking maybe he got
a little lost in the role.

221
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:38,250
See. He can't resolve
those facets of himself.

222
00:14:38,280 --> 00:14:40,450
Can't bear the weight
of what he's done.

223
00:14:40,520 --> 00:14:42,480
The only way for him
to manage his conscience

224
00:14:42,520 --> 00:14:45,250
is to fall for his own act.

225
00:14:45,290 --> 00:14:48,420
He thinks he is a soldier.

226
00:14:48,460 --> 00:14:51,430
This is what you call
a split personality.

227
00:14:51,460 --> 00:14:53,130
He's gone insane.

228
00:14:53,200 --> 00:14:55,360
His heart and mind
are at war with each other,

229
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:57,670
and judging by
Bertholdt's expression,

230
00:14:57,730 --> 00:15:01,200
this isn't the first stalemate.

231
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:02,940
Blows me away!

232
00:15:02,970 --> 00:15:05,740
Wow, someone as brutally honest
as you losing their grip--

233
00:15:05,780 --> 00:15:11,750
[REINER]
Shut up! Not another word.

234
00:15:13,550 --> 00:15:17,890
I'm sorry.
Must've really hit a nerve.

235
00:15:21,390 --> 00:15:24,790
[EREN]
Is this some kind of joke?

236
00:15:24,830 --> 00:15:27,900
Where do you get off
pretending to be the victim?

237
00:15:27,960 --> 00:15:30,730
You're wallowing in self-pity?

238
00:15:30,770 --> 00:15:34,270
How dare you. What was
going through your head

239
00:15:34,300 --> 00:15:37,170
the day I told you
my story, huh?

240
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:39,610
Remember that, Bertholdt?

241
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:42,680
I'm talking to you, lackey!

242
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:44,910
I told you everything.

243
00:15:44,950 --> 00:15:47,620
You sat there and looked me
straight in the eye.

244
00:15:47,650 --> 00:15:50,580
Watched me relive seeing
my mother eaten alive.

245
00:15:50,620 --> 00:15:53,990
[EREN]
Stop it! No!

246
00:15:54,020 --> 00:15:55,690
Don't you remember?

247
00:15:55,760 --> 00:15:57,590
Well, it just so happens
the chunk of wall

248
00:15:57,630 --> 00:15:59,690
you kicked out
fell on our house.

249
00:15:59,760 --> 00:16:03,200
It's what kept her from
being able to run away.

250
00:16:03,270 --> 00:16:07,970
Ring any bells? Take you back?

251
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,300
Let me ask you again.

252
00:16:10,340 --> 00:16:15,780
What was going through your head
when I told you that story?

253
00:16:18,210 --> 00:16:21,650
Want me to be honest?

254
00:16:21,680 --> 00:16:25,950
In the moment I felt...
sorry for you.

255
00:16:30,190 --> 00:16:35,560
[EREN]
Huh. Sorry for me?

256
00:16:35,630 --> 00:16:39,400
So, then. You're not...

257
00:16:39,470 --> 00:16:45,710
You're not warriors or soldiers.
You're just murderers.

258
00:16:45,740 --> 00:16:48,310
Psychotic mass-murderers
who snuffed out the lives

259
00:16:48,340 --> 00:16:50,640
of countless people that
never did you any wrong.

260
00:16:50,680 --> 00:16:52,510
Don't you think
I'm aware of that fact?

261
00:16:52,550 --> 00:16:55,020
I don't need you shoving it
down my goddamn throat!

262
00:16:55,050 --> 00:16:56,820
Then stop acting
like you've got any right

263
00:16:56,850 --> 00:16:58,590
to feel sorry for yourself!

264
00:16:58,650 --> 00:17:01,090
We're living in a hell
you two created!

265
00:17:01,160 --> 00:17:02,560
Are you proud of yourselves?

266
00:17:02,590 --> 00:17:04,330
You're not one of us!
You've never been!

267
00:17:04,390 --> 00:17:06,430
You're not even human anymore!

268
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:07,900
[REINER]
You want an apology?

269
00:17:07,960 --> 00:17:09,930
Is that what you hope to get
out of calling us murderers?

270
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:12,700
Want us to feel bad?
Want us to take the blame?

271
00:17:12,740 --> 00:17:14,540
Who are you talking to?

272
00:17:14,570 --> 00:17:16,400
The people you thought
you knew don't exist!

273
00:17:16,440 --> 00:17:19,410
They're dead! But hey,
if screaming does it for ya,

274
00:17:19,440 --> 00:17:23,040
go ahead and scream
your goddamn head off!

275
00:17:26,250 --> 00:17:35,560
[REINER panting]

276
00:17:35,590 --> 00:17:37,960
[EREN]
You're right.

277
00:17:38,030 --> 00:17:43,860
Who am I? What do I know?

278
00:17:43,900 --> 00:17:50,770
Still. I've got to do
something. Anything.

279
00:17:50,870 --> 00:17:53,270
I swear to you,
one way or another,

280
00:17:53,310 --> 00:17:58,450
the two of you will pay.
And it's gonna hurt.

281
00:18:05,820 --> 00:18:08,260
[YMIR]
You can't be for real.

282
00:18:08,290 --> 00:18:09,790
Huh?

283
00:18:09,830 --> 00:18:12,290
Eren, grow up.
Keep spouting off

284
00:18:12,330 --> 00:18:15,930
childish bullshit like that
and I've got no hope for you.

285
00:18:15,970 --> 00:18:18,070
[EREN grunts]

286
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:22,540
[YMIR]
Tell me something.

287
00:18:24,910 --> 00:18:27,240
What's with the giant monkey?

288
00:18:30,410 --> 00:18:33,080
[REINER] Monkey?
What're you talking about?

289
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:36,150
Huh. I thought
for sure you'd know.

290
00:18:36,190 --> 00:18:39,190
That's surprising. From the way
you guys were ogling it

291
00:18:39,260 --> 00:18:41,020
all slack-jawed
I figured we were seeing

292
00:18:41,090 --> 00:18:43,290
some kind of living legend.

293
00:18:43,330 --> 00:18:45,330
Weird.

294
00:18:45,360 --> 00:18:48,360
A monkey? Don't be cute.

295
00:18:48,430 --> 00:18:52,030
Shut up and listen.
Monkey, Beast Titan.

296
00:18:52,100 --> 00:18:56,100
Whatever you wanna call him,
he's behind this latest fiasco.

297
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:59,440
It's why Titans are
cropping up out of nowhere.

298
00:18:59,480 --> 00:19:04,040
I get the feeling
he's gauging our strength.

299
00:19:04,110 --> 00:19:07,310
Reiner and Betholdt are
trying to get wherever he is.

300
00:19:07,350 --> 00:19:09,380
It's how they're
getting back home.

301
00:19:09,450 --> 00:19:12,050
Feel free to correct me
if I'm way off base.

302
00:19:12,120 --> 00:19:13,190
[Gasps]

303
00:19:13,220 --> 00:19:16,720
Wait. How did you know?
Who are you?

304
00:19:16,790 --> 00:19:18,360
What else haven't you told me?

305
00:19:18,390 --> 00:19:21,730
Be patient. I'm caught up
in circumstances of my own.

306
00:19:21,800 --> 00:19:24,530
What the hell is that
supposed to mean?

307
00:19:24,570 --> 00:19:26,900
Eren. If you think
killing these morons

308
00:19:26,970 --> 00:19:30,840
will put an end to all of this,
you are sorely mistaken.

309
00:19:30,870 --> 00:19:33,640
[EREN]
Huh? But then who's the enemy?

310
00:19:33,680 --> 00:19:35,040
The enemy?

311
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,810
Look, if I told you,
things would get too--

312
00:19:36,850 --> 00:19:41,080
[REINER] Ymir! There's no future
for this world and you know it.

313
00:19:41,150 --> 00:19:42,380
[YMIR gasps]

314
00:19:42,490 --> 00:19:44,050
[REINER] You have
a solid grasp of things.

315
00:19:44,090 --> 00:19:45,820
What d'you think comes next?

316
00:19:45,860 --> 00:19:47,920
Joining our side wouldn't
be out of the question

317
00:19:47,990 --> 00:19:50,060
if you were so inclined.

318
00:19:50,090 --> 00:19:53,030
[YMIR] And put my faith
in you guys? That's rich.

319
00:19:53,060 --> 00:19:55,700
Neither of you trusts me
as far as you can throw me.

320
00:19:55,730 --> 00:19:58,570
[REINER]
Come on. That isn't true.

321
00:19:58,670 --> 00:20:01,240
We know what you really want.

322
00:20:01,270 --> 00:20:04,070
All you care about
is protecting Christa.

323
00:20:05,940 --> 00:20:10,040
If we can all agree on that,
I don't see the conflict.

324
00:20:10,080 --> 00:20:12,580
I'm being absolutely serious.

325
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:16,020
Is it so hard to believe we
want what's best for her, too?

326
00:20:16,050 --> 00:20:18,920
Hate to break it to ya,
but you're not the only one.

327
00:20:18,950 --> 00:20:22,020
Then again, you could always
put your trust in Eren,

328
00:20:22,060 --> 00:20:24,190
see where that leads you.

329
00:20:24,230 --> 00:20:25,730
What?

330
00:20:28,700 --> 00:20:31,070
[REINER] You're probably
leaning toward escape.

331
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:34,570
Better to take a chance with him
than throw in with us, right?

332
00:20:34,600 --> 00:20:36,440
Because if we
end up taking you,

333
00:20:36,470 --> 00:20:39,640
there's not much hope
of being rescued.

334
00:20:39,710 --> 00:20:42,610
I'll be straight with you.
That much is true.

335
00:20:42,650 --> 00:20:44,910
Even if you came willingly,
we're not in a position

336
00:20:44,950 --> 00:20:47,550
to guarantee your safety.

337
00:20:47,580 --> 00:20:49,880
But if it's Christa
we're talking about,

338
00:20:49,920 --> 00:20:51,450
we might be able
to do something.

339
00:20:51,490 --> 00:20:54,890
[YMIR Gasps and snarls]

340
00:20:54,920 --> 00:20:57,290
[REINER] It's your call.
What's it gonna be?

341
00:20:57,330 --> 00:21:03,160
Is it Christa's future?
Or your own petty existence?

342
00:21:03,230 --> 00:21:05,930
[EREN] Is there really
no future for this world?

343
00:21:05,970 --> 00:21:08,570
Why? And the monkey.

344
00:21:08,600 --> 00:21:11,440
How does he figure into this?

345
00:21:11,470 --> 00:21:14,780
Come clean!
Who's the real enemy?

346
00:21:14,810 --> 00:21:18,080
Tell me what you know!

347
00:21:18,110 --> 00:21:20,450
Who is it?!

348
00:21:22,850 --> 00:21:26,850
[YMIR sighs]

349
00:21:26,920 --> 00:21:28,320
Couldn't say.

350
00:21:28,360 --> 00:21:29,660
[EREN grunts]

351
00:21:29,690 --> 00:21:33,490
[REINER]
All right, then. Sorry, Eren.

352
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,660
[Distant gunshot]

353
00:21:43,870 --> 00:21:47,780
[BERTHOLDT]
The Scouts are here? Already?

354
00:21:47,810 --> 00:21:50,840
[REINER grunts]
Son of a bitch!

355
00:21:50,950 --> 00:21:55,550
[EREN]
No. Damn you, Ymir!

356
00:21:57,990 --> 00:22:01,820
[EREN] Only one hour
left until sunset.

357
00:22:09,930 --> 00:22:14,940
♪ Closing Song
